title: Btrfs Filesystem
agents: linux
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the disk usage of redundant btrfs volumes (RAID1, RAID5,
 RAID6, RAID10, dup) using corrected values. On such profiles, the standard
 "Filesystem" check reports an inflated usage (size - avail) because of the
 redundancy ratio, even though only a few GiB of data are actually stored.

 The agent plug-in {btrfs_df} detects redundant btrfs volumes and sends
 size = real_data + avail, so that Checkmk's standard formula
 (used = size - avail) reports the real data usage instead.

 The service keeps the same features as the built-in "Filesystem" check:
 graph, trend, "full in X days", inodes and the same "Filesystem levels"
 rule (thresholds based on used space).

item:
 The mountpoint of the volume (e.g. {/mnt/data-raid5}).

discovery:
 One service {Btrfs Filesystem <mountpoint>} is created for every redundant
 btrfs volume reported by the {btrfs_df} agent section.
